{
	title: 'Web client on SolidJS 2',
	spec: `src/web is a SolidJS 2 app with every feature the plain-DOM page had: password login, one session's transcript folded by common transcript.fold, streamed output, pending prompts and the inbox, drafts kept in localStorage (common/drafts.ts), questions answered through forms.step, the model picker modal, editing the last prompt (common/amend.ts), slash completion, reconnect with backoff and a fresh snapshot. page.ts is gone.

Why a dependency: the page is about to grow (tabs, collapsible cards, animations, prompt editing, image paste) and hand-written DOM patching already ran page.ts past 400 lines. Solid updates exactly the DOM a signal feeds, with no virtual DOM and a small runtime; the previous Hal chose it over React as smaller and less error-prone. Only the browser uses it.

The host path stays dependency-free. No module in host, client or common imports solid-js, @solidjs/web or @solidjs/compiler statically; the conventions test checks that for every non-web layer. host/web.ts bundles the page with Bun.build and compiles .tsx with @solidjs/compiler through a Bun plugin (artifact solid-build-excerpt.ts), imported dynamically on the first GET /, so a host that never serves the page never loads it; a missing or broken compiler answers that request with 500 and a diag.log line and never harms the host.

Conventions (update the web section of tasks/README.md): components are .tsx files in src/web/components/, one exported component each, whose root element has a class named after it; decisions (key mapping, view state, reconnect, scroll maths) stay in plain .ts modules unit-tested without a browser; src/web imports only web and common. The browser gets its colours only from the CSS the host generates from src/common/colors.ts (task 1w): no colour literals in src/web or index.html (add fields to colors.ts for what is missing); layout CSS lives in one stylesheet. The conventions test covers .tsx files (layers, side-effect-free import, the 400-line limit); take src/web/page.ts off the size exception list. The CDP end-to-end check in host/web.test.ts still logs in and sees a streamed answer. The web.md artifact reflects the current browser status layout: task a0's compact two-line overview with native modal details and no duplicate activity row above the composer. The guide also describes task cw's native short-landscape typography and visual-viewport draft-height cap.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'This reverses dz\'s "plain DOM, no framework" choice (and the README line saying so) on purpose; dz\'s other rules stand.',
		'Current web implementation guide: tasks/1b/web.md. Read it before writing src/web code; old-web.md is a historical artifact rather than the normative guide. The guide distinguishes displayed data, pending replacements and absence, and requires retaining DOM and value identity when an async reply confirms the visible result. Task kx applies it to completion menus.',
		'Solid 2 is not Solid 1: createEffect takes (compute, apply); onSettled replaces onMount; no createResource or batch (writes are microtask-batched, flush() at imperative boundaries); class arrays, not classList; <For keyed={false}> gives an item accessor and index; writing a signal inside a component body or memo throws REACTIVE_WRITE_IN_OWNED_SCOPE.',
		'Bun resolves solid-js to its server build by default and it fails silently (memos never recompute). Tests that import Solid need `bun test --conditions browser --conditions development`; bunfig.toml conditions were ignored in the old Hal. Sanity check: createMemo(() => c() * 2) sees setC(5) after flush(). Keep most tests Solid-free by keeping logic in .ts modules.',
		"The old Hal pinned solid-js and @solidjs/web 2.0.0-rc.0 with @dom-expressions/compiler 0.50.0-next.40, compiled with transform(source, { filename, moduleName: '@solidjs/web', generate: 'dom' }). Newer 2.0 prereleases may exist; pin a pair that works together, exact versions, and update them together.",
		'tsconfig needs jsx: preserve and jsxImportSource: @solidjs/web. Keep DOM types out of host code: page.ts used /// <reference lib="dom" />; a per-file reference or a src/web tsconfig both work.',
		"Keep dz's notes: format iife (esm output breaks an inline classic script), the /*APP*/ and /*COLORS*/ substitution into index.html, and the bundle cached until server.stop().",
		"old-main.tsx is the old Hal's app shell, for reference only: its protocol and state differ from hal2's. The previous page's behaviour (view.ts, link.ts and their tests) is the spec.",
		'Pinned: solid-js and @solidjs/web 2.0.0-rc.8, @solidjs/signals 2.0.0-rc.8 (package.json overrides), @dom-expressions/compiler 0.50.0-next.44, the newest compiler. rc.9 renamed the delegated-event key from $$ to _$$ while the compiler still emits $$, so onInput/onClick silently never fire; signals rc.10 under solid-js rc.8 blanked the page. Check a delegated event in the browser after any upgrade.',
		"Bun imports .tsx with its own React-style JSX (jsxDEV), and Solid's server build throws on DOM templates, so the conventions side-effect test loads every module with `bun --conditions browser` after Bun.plugin(await web.plugin()).",
		'app.ts is the controller: plain state changed synchronously, then app.changed() (Chat.tsx sets it to a signal write). Page keys go through one document keydown listener to app.key with a Target (message box text and caret, field, button); it flush()es afterwards so the DOM shows the outcome before the next event.',
		"One snapshot signal means every redraw reaches every component. Chat gates it with one createMemo per field (default === equality; pending, a fresh array each time, compares contents), so typing reaches only the composer. Without this gate, typing re-rendered the transcript and (with 4s's fallback bug) remounted every card. Solid ships its own guide at node_modules/solid-js/skills/reactivity-diagnostics/SKILL.md: read UNSTABLE_MEMO_OUTPUT, UNSTABLE_LIST_IDENTITY and HOT_SCOPE_RERUNS before adding state plumbing.",
		'The page\'s own surfaces (canvas, text, accent, field, border, button) are the colors.page style, custom properties on <html class="page">.',
		'The CDP test in host/web.test.ts also answers a question (/cd to a missing directory), opens and closes the picker, and checks a typed draft survives a reload: that last check is what catches dead delegated events.',
		'Render only what changed (tasks/README.md, Web client): the user asked the old Hal "every live update creates new transcript-item objects? Live update should update that object in place and Solid\'s signals handle the rest". Two ways that work: one signal gated by a memo per field (what Chat does), or a store the host\'s data is merged into with reconcile(data, key) inside a draft setter (old-web.md, Reactivity), which keeps object identity so keyed lists and memos see no change. Don\'t replace a whole snapshot object and let every consumer recompute.',
		"A host restart or dropped socket leaves the page's DOM alive: show reconnecting, reconnect, fold the fresh snapshot into the same cards. Never reload on a fixed delay (old Hal commit 601e442: that stranded the installed iOS app on a blank page); if a reload is ever needed, probe HTTP first and only after pending draft writes are durable.",
